---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Astrophysics Cheat Sheet | Free Stars, Galaxies, Cosmology"
  description="Complete astrophysics cheat sheet with stars, galaxies, and cosmology. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Astrophysics<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Stars, galaxies, and cosmology. From stellar evolution to Big Bang theory.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Stellar Properties</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Luminosity & Flux</h3>
        <pre><code>L = 4πR²σT⁴ (Stefan-Boltzmann)
F = L/(4πd²) (flux)
M = -2.5 log(L/L₀) (absolute magnitude)
m - M = 5 log(d/10) (distance modulus)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Wien's Law</h3>
        <pre><code>λ_max T = 2.898 × 10⁻³ m·K
Peak wavelength × temperature = constant</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Stellar Evolution</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>HR Diagram</h3>
        <pre><code>x-axis: Temperature (decreasing right)
y-axis: Luminosity (increasing up)
Main sequence: most stars
Red giants: cool, luminous
White dwarfs: hot, dim</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>End States</h3>
        <pre><code>Low mass (< 8 M_sun): white dwarf
Medium mass (8-25 M_sun): neutron star
High mass (> 25 M_sun): black hole
Chandrasekhar limit: 1.4 MM_sun
Tolman-Oppenheimer-Volkoff limit: ~3 MM_sun</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cosmology</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Hubble's Law</h3>
        <pre><code>v = H₀d
v = recession velocity
d = distance
H₀ = 70 km/s/Mpc</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Big Bang</h3>
        <pre><code>CMB: 2.725 K (cosmic microwave background)
Age: ~13.8 billion years
Composition: 5% ordinary, 27% dark matter, 68% dark energy</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
